flowchart TB
accTitle: Four CoALA memory responsibilities and their distinct retrieval filters
accDescr: Working memory is fetched by id and checked for scope and expiry, not reconstructed historically. Episodic retrieval filters by scope, optional entity, and known time. Semantic retrieval occurs only with an entity and filters by valid time and known time. Procedural retrieval filters by scope and known time. Each store applies its own rules; historically eligible records may still be returned with their currently stored superseded or retired status. The typed result may later feed B1 selection and B3 admission, which are separate operations.

    WM[Working memory<br/>identifier, scope, expiry<br/>current stored snapshot]
    EP[Episodic memory<br/>verified at known time<br/>optional entity filter]
    SM[Semantic memory<br/>only when entity supplied<br/>valid time + known time]
    PM[Procedural memory<br/>active at known time<br/>no valid-time filter]
    WM --> RET[Cross-store retrieval<br/>per-store filters and limits]
    EP --> RET
    SM --> RET
    PM --> RET
    RET --> RESULT[Typed retrieval result<br/>current stored objects]
    RESULT -. later selection .-> B1[B1 memory selection<br/>Chapter 21]
    B1 -. later admission .-> B3[B3 workspace<br/>Chapter 21]
